Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `scientificname`: filter to rows that belong to the species Sterna paradisaea  
• `species`: second possibility to identify the same species (use together with, or instead of, scientificname)  
• `decimallatitude`: make sure the sighting was north of 40° latitude ( > 40)  
• `year`, `month`, `day`: build calendar dates, filter out January (month > 1) and let us sort chronologically  
• `eventdate`: an already‑assembled timestamp that may help check that the three integer columns line up correctly  
• `gbifid` (any non‑null column): can be used for simple counts (`COUNT(*) AS sightings`)  

Typical conditions that will be necessary  
1. LOWER(`scientificname`) LIKE '%sterna paradisaea%'  (or use `species` = 'Sterna paradisaea')  
2. `decimallatitude` > 40  
3. `month` > 1                                    -- “after January”  
4. GROUP BY (`year`,`month`,`day`) HAVING COUNT(*) > 10  

